  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most important uncertainty is whether a basic multimodal setup provides a viable performance baseline for this task. config_002 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) is the simplest, most standard multimodal configuration: it uses well-established pretrained encoders (ImageNet ViT-L for images, scVI for RNA), the simplest profile setting (singleprofile), and the simplest fusion (concat), avoiding confounding from aggregation or weighted fusion. This establishes a reference performance against which all more complex multimodal variants (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) and unimodal baselines (image-only, RNA-only) can later be compared. Testing the simplest multimodal setup first is the highest-information use of the first experiment: if it performs well, we validate the multimodal hypothesis and can exploit by exploring which added complexity helps; if it underperforms, we learn that the basic fusion or encoder choice is the bottleneck before investing in more complex configurations."
}

